    "result_text": "All tests pass (7 tests across the suite, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the derived `ownerSegment` field following the codebase's established pattern for read-only derived owner attributes (like `locality`, `contactPreference`, `ageBand`): pure logic lives in a small `model` class, the `OwnerMapper` delegates to it, and the field is declared in `openapi.yml` (from which `OwnerDto` is generated).\n\n**New: `model/OwnerSegment.java`** \u2014 owns the segment logic, composing two independent axes as nested enums, each with a single responsibility:\n- `Tier.of(membershipLevel)` \u2192 `PREMIUM` when level \u2265 3 (`PREMIUM_MIN_LEVEL`), else `STANDARD`.\n- `Area.of(locality)` \u2192 `METRO` for a known region, else `REGIONAL`.\n- `OwnerSegment.of(membershipLevel, locality)` \u2192 `\"<TIER>_<AREA>\"`.\n\nIt takes the already-derived `membershipLevel` and `locality` scalars rather than re-deriving them, so it stays decoupled from `Owner` and reuses the existing derivation the mapper already performs.\n\n**`model/CityRegion.java`** \u2014 added `isKnownRegion(String region)`, keeping \"what counts as a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD)\" in the class that already owns the region reference data, rather than hardcoding the check in `OwnerSegment`.\n\n**`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `ownerSegment(owner)` default method delegating to `OwnerSegment.of(membershipLevel(owner), locality(owner))`, reusing the existing `membershipLevel` and `locality` helpers, plus the `@Mapping` entry and import.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `ownerSegment` read-only string property (documented with the four allowed values), matching how the other fixed-value derived strings are modeled (plain string, not a generated enum type).",
